# A program that asks for focus reports (DEC mode 1004 — vim's
# FocusGained / FocusLost and `autoread`, neovim, helix, lazygit) hears
# `ESC [ O` when its pane loses the focus and `ESC [ I` when it gets it
# back, as ghostty sends them per surface and tmux per pane.
#
# The child switches 1004 on and records what it reads next; a click
# into the editor above, then back into the terminal.
write a.txt "x\n"
open a.txt
command view.toggle_tree
shell printf '%s\n' 'stty raw -echo; printf "\033[?1004h"; dd bs=1 count=6 2>/dev/null | od -An -c > focus.txt; stty sane; sleep 20' > f.sh
ex term sh f.sh
wait 800
click 10 5
wait 300
click 10 30
wait 800
expect file focus.txt contains "O"
expect file focus.txt contains "I"
